(7703116, 1264724, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Love the perspective in this shot! Who hasn''t taken a break sitting on the dock dangling one''s feet over the edge - the activity is very relatable that one can easily put themselves in the picture. I like that this composition has the bridge reflected on the water''s surface for it adds visual interest. It plays with the mind as to what is up and what is down. I do wonder what this looks like in color in that if the water reflects blue sky and white clouds that would compliment the mood of relaxation more so than B&amp;W.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Love the perspective in this shot! Who hasn''t taken a break sitting on the dock dangling one''s feet over the edge - the activity is very relatable that one can easily put themselves in the picture. I like that this composition has the bridge reflected on the water''s surface for it adds visual interest. It plays with the mind as to what is up and what is down. I do wonder what this looks like in color in that if the water reflects blue sky and white clouds that would compliment the mood of relaxation more so than B&W.', '2021-10-11 09:30:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(7703117, 1264762, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Wow! That blue hue of the iceberg and the mountains off in distance is stunning! Very beautiful! I do have one suggestion to improve visual impact of image - bring the viewer closer to the main subject. Cropping to landscape orientation with the bottom being just under the reflection of that blue iceberg not only brings the viewer closer to the stunning beauty of the place but it also compliments and follows the shape/line/orientation of the iceberg.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Wow! That blue hue of the iceberg and the mountains off in distance is stunning! Very beautiful! I do have one suggestion to improve visual impact of image - bring the viewer closer to the main subject. Cropping to landscape orientation with the bottom being just under the reflection of that blue iceberg not only brings the viewer closer to the stunning beauty of the place but it also compliments and follows the shape/line/orientation of the iceberg.', '2021-10-11 09:35:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(7703118, 1264763, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Ah Venice! The colors of the Acqua Alta draws the eye in as does the waves. I have a suggestion on how to increase visual impact of the photo. Crop out the wall with the single window on the left leaving only the arched door and all the exposed brick wall on the right. As it is now there are too many elements that draw the eyes attention. Focus your audience''s attention to where they will stay, linger, and wonder what lies beyond the arched doorway once the waters recede.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Ah Venice! The colors of the Acqua Alta draws the eye in as does the waves. I have a suggestion on how to increase visual impact of the photo. Crop out the wall with the single window on the left leaving only the arched door and all the exposed brick wall on the right. As it is now there are too many elements that draw the eyes attention. Focus your audience''s attention to where they will stay, linger, and wonder what lies beyond the arched doorway once the waters recede.', '2021-10-11 09:48:06.000000', NULL, 1),
